# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Admin dashboard environment
#
# Every VITE_* value is visible in the browser bundle. The only
# thing this app needs to know is where the API is.
#
# There is deliberately no Supabase key, no Cloudinary key and
# no admin credential here. Sessions are HTTP-only cookies the
# JavaScript cannot read, issued by the Backend.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Local development only. There is no rewrite in front of `vite dev`, so the
# dashboard needs the API's absolute address here.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000

# Shown behind the sidebar's "View website" link. Public information.
VITE_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ── VITE_API_BASE_URL IS DEVELOPMENT-ONLY ───────────────────
#
# A production build IGNORES it: the compiled dashboard always
# calls its own origin, and `vercel.json` rewrites /api/* to the
# API deployment. So the browser only ever talks to the dashboard's
# own hostname and the session cookie is FIRST-PARTY.
#
# Setting it on Vercel does nothing, and it is clearer to delete it
# there. The API's address belongs in `vercel.json` — one place,
# which cannot silently disagree with a second one.
#
# This is not a preference. If the dashboard called the API on a
# separate domain (madhuri-jewellary-backend.vercel.app), the
# session cookie would be a THIRD-PARTY cookie, and:
#
#   - Chrome Incognito blocks it by default  -> login bounces
#     straight back to /login, every time
#   - Safari (ITP) blocks it
#   - Firefox partitions it
#   - Chrome is phasing it out for normal windows too
#
# No cookie attribute can override that; SameSite=None and Secure
# are necessary for cross-site cookies but are ignored once the
# browser has decided not to accept third-party cookies at all.
#
# Set the API's hostname in AdminFrontend/vercel.json instead.
